{% set design %}
<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-usage">Usage</h2>
  <p>The auth shell is a one-purpose frame: a centered card on a plain page,
     nothing else. No app chrome — auth is a <em>pre-app</em> screen with
     nothing to navigate to, so there is no top bar and no nav. The card and
     its fields are part of the shell, not separate components.</p>
  <h3>Do use it when</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Sign-in, sign-up, password reset, MFA challenge — any single form screen
        reached before the app shell.</li>
    <li>You want the form to work without JS — it's a plain <code>&lt;form&gt;</code>
        posting anywhere you like.</li>
    <li>Consistency with the app shells matters — same tokens, same flat
        borders.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Don't use it when</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>The screen has navigation or multiple destinations — use a real shell.</li>
    <li>You need form controls beyond text inputs (selects, toggles) — the field
        styles cover inputs only; the planned 0.2 components extend this.</li>
    <li>The flow is multi-step with progress indication — wrap your own step
        indicator inside the card.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

