<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-behavior">Behavior</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Zero JS:</strong> no <code>flint.js</code> needed — the card is a real form; submit posts wherever the <code>action</code> says.</li>
    <li><strong>One breakpoint:</strong> the card is fluid and centers at every width; under 600px the card's side margins and padding shrink. No layout flip.</li>
    <li><strong>Field states:</strong> hover darkens the border, focus takes the accent border, invalid (native <code>:invalid</code>) is styled too — all in CSS.</li>
    <li><strong>Card width:</strong> capped at ~400px — long forms should split across screens, not widen the card.</li>
    <li><strong>No app chrome:</strong> no top bar, no nav, no JS — there is nothing to navigate to before authentication. After sign-in, hand off to a real shell (drawer, rail, or bottom-nav).</li>
    <li><strong>Branding:</strong> no logo slot by default — add your wordmark or an <code>&lt;img&gt;</code> above the title inside the card if you want one; it needs no library CSS.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Each field is a <code>&lt;label class="fl-field"&gt;</code> wrapping its input — the label association is structural, no <code>for</code>/<code>id</code> needed.</li>
    <li>Use the right <code>autocomplete</code> tokens (<code>email</code>, <code>current-password</code>, <code>new-password</code>) — password managers and the HTML spec both expect them.</li>
    <li>The card is a <code>&lt;form&gt;</code> and its title is the page's <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code> — with no app chrome there is no other heading, so the hierarchy starts right at "Sign in".</li>
    <li>Errors: use native validation first (<code>required</code>, <code>type</code>); server errors should be announced with <code>role="alert"</code> text inside the card.</li>
    <li>Focus order is natural (DOM order); <code>:focus-visible</code> gets the accent ring.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
{% endset %}

